Q8:
Why is it recommended to use ApplicationContext instead of Activity Context in some cases? Give an example.

A:
Context gives access to app resources, services, etc.
Activity Context is tied to the Activity lifecycle. Holding it in long-lived objects (like singletons, Adapters, or background tasks) can cause memory leaks if the Activity is destroyed but the reference remains.

ApplicationContext lives for the entire lifetime of the app.
Example: Initializing a Room database, setting up Glide image loader, or creating a singleton Logger. These don’t need Activity-specific resources so ApplicationContext is safer.

