Q11:
Explain the role of Intents in Android. What is the difference between an explicit and an implicit Intent? Give an example of each.

A:
Intents are messages used to request an action from another app component or another app.
- Explicit Intent: Directly specifies the target component’s class name. Used within your app.
  Example: Starting SecondActivity from MainActivity using `Intent intent = new Intent(this, SecondActivity.class);`
- Implicit Intent: Does not name a specific component. System finds a matching component that can handle the action.
  Example: Sharing an image: `Intent intent = new Intent(Intent.ACTION_SEND)` with MIME type set.

