Q22:
Describe how the Android architecture components (ViewModel, LiveData, Room, WorkManager) work together to build a robust app. Provide a concrete example flow.

A:
These Jetpack components simplify app architecture:

- ViewModel: Holds UI-related data, survives configuration changes.
- LiveData: Observable data holder, lifecycle-aware.
- Room: SQLite ORM, abstracts database with compile-time checks.
- WorkManager: Schedules guaranteed background work respecting constraints.

Example flow:  
User adds a Note →  
- UI calls ViewModel's addNote() method →  
- ViewModel calls Repository →  
- Repository inserts note into Room database →  
- LiveData observes database changes →  
- UI updates automatically →  
- WorkManager schedules background sync to upload notes.

Code snippets:

ViewModel:

public class NoteViewModel extends ViewModel {
    private LiveData<List<Note>> notes;
    private NoteRepository repository;

    public NoteViewModel() {
        repository = new NoteRepository();
        notes = repository.getAllNotes();
    }

    public LiveData<List<Note>> getNotes() {
        return notes;
    }

    public void addNote(Note note) {
        repository.insert(note);
    }
}

Room DAO:

@Dao
public interface NoteDao {
    @Query("SELECT * FROM notes")
    LiveData<List<Note>> getAllNotes();

    @Insert
    void insert(Note note);
}

WorkManager setup for sync:

public class SyncWorker extends Worker {
    public SyncWorker(@NonNull Context context, @NonNull WorkerParameters params) {
        super(context, params);
    }

    @NonNull
    @Override
    public Result doWork() {
        // Upload notes to server
        return Result.success();
    }
}

// Schedule
WorkManager workManager = WorkManager.getInstance(context);
PeriodicWorkRequest syncRequest = new PeriodicWorkRequest.Builder(SyncWorker.class, 12, TimeUnit.HOURS)
    .setConstraints(new Constraints.Builder()
        .setRequiredNetworkType(NetworkType.UNMETERED)
        .build())
    .build();
workManager.enqueueUniquePeriodicWork("notes_sync", ExistingPeriodicWorkPolicy.KEEP, syncRequest);

